.TH PALETTE 2
.SH NAME
xrgb,
mix,
shade,
by_name \- the one palette
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B import "vsys:libpal"
.PP
.nf
.B "RGB :: [3]u8"
.fi
.PP
.nf
.B "xrgb :: proc(c: RGB) -> u32"
.B "mix :: proc(a: RGB, b: RGB, t: u8) -> RGB"
.B "shade :: proc(c: RGB, amount: i16) -> RGB"
.B "by_name :: proc(name: string) -> (RGB, bool)"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Libpal
is Vectra's one system palette, named "Cyberpunk Workstation 1994": the
colours of the boot splash, the panic screen and the desktop, so that
all three are visibly the same machine.
Both privilege levels read it.
The kernel's
.IR fb (3)
aliases every name here and adds the surface painters a kernel device
needs.
A ring 3 program packs a colour into a pixel word with
.IR xrgb .
.PP
An
.B RGB
is three bytes, red, green and blue, each from 0 to 255.
The palette itself is a set of named constants, not procedures: surfaces
.RB ( VOID ,
.BR SLATE_DEEP ,
.BR SLATE ,
.B MAGNESIUM_DARK
through
.BR MAGNESIUM_HOT ),
copper trim
.RB ( COPPER_DARK ,
.BR COPPER ,
.BR COPPER_LIT ),
and four phosphor accents, each with a dim and (for amber) a hot
variant:
.BR AMBER ,
.BR CYAN ,
.BR PHOSPHOR ,
and
.BR ALERT .
.PP
.I Xrgb
packs a colour into the 32-bit pixel word ring 3 draws with: the low 8
bits blue, the next 8 green, the next 8 red.
.IR Libdraw 's
command stream and
.BR /srv/draw
carry pixels in exactly this layout, and accept no other depth.
.PP
.I Mix
blends two colours,
.I t
parts in 255 of the way from
.I a
to
.IR b .
.I Shade
lightens or darkens one colour by
.I amount ,
saturating rather than wrapping at black or white, which is how a
bevel's two edges come from one face colour.
.PP
.I By_name
resolves one of the palette's own names, lower case with an underscore
where the constant has one
.RI ( "for example" ,
.BR magnesium_lit ),
to its
.BR RGB .
It answers
.B false
for a name the table does not carry, which a caller reads as "try six
hex digits instead".
It is how a theme file
(see
.IR theme (6))
names a role's colour in words.
.SH SOURCE
.B sys/libpal/palette.odin
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR fb (3),
.IR draw (2),
.IR theme (6),
.IR mui (2)
